# Project Structure Guide

LLAE is organized into several key directories:

## Core Directories
- `scripts/` - Contains the core Lua modules
  - `llae/` - Core functionality modules
  - `net/` - Networking modules including HTTP and WebSocket
  - `web/` - Web framework modules
  - `db/` - Database clients (Redis, PostgreSQL)

## Documentation
- `docs/` - Module documentation in Markdown format
  - `db/` - Database modules documentation
  - `net/` - Network modules documentation
  - `web.md` - Web framework documentation
  - `cli.md` - CLI commands documentation

## Examples
The [examples/](mdc:examples) directory contains working examples for various features:
- [examples/app.lua](mdc:examples/app.lua) - Complete web application example
- [examples/http.lua](mdc:examples/http.lua) - HTTP server example
- [examples/redis.lua](mdc:examples/redis.lua) - Redis client example
- [examples/pgsql.lua](mdc:examples/pgsql.lua) - PostgreSQL client example
- [examples/websocket.lua](mdc:examples/websocket.lua) - WebSocket example

## Tools
- `tools/` - CLI command implementations
  - [tools/commands.lua](mdc:tools/commands.lua) - Command registry
  - Individual command modules like `install.lua`, `run.lua`, etc.

## Project Files
- `llae-project.lua` - Project configuration file
- `bin/llae` - Main executable

## Unit tests
The `tests/` directory constains unit tests.
Unit tests framework is luaunit.
Important: command for run tests is: `./bin/llae run tests`
